/**
@mainpage Vigil API Reference

Vigil is a cross-platform endpoint detection agent. The public API is split into
small runtime components:

- @ref vigil::EventCollector collects process snapshots and emits process events.
- @ref vigil::RuleEngine evaluates process snapshots and emits alerts.
- @ref vigil::Config loads rule configuration from platform-specific JSON files.
- @ref vigil::ProcessInfo is the normalized cross-platform process snapshot used by rules.

Typical embedding flow:

@code{.cpp}
auto config = vigil::Config::loadFromFile("config/platform/windows/config.json");
auto collector = vigil::createEventCollector();
auto engine = vigil::createRuleEngine(config);

collector->onProcess.connect([&](const vigil::ProcessInfo& process) {
   engine->process(process);
});

engine->onAlert.connect([](const vigil::Alert& alert) {
   vigil::log::warn("{}: pid={}", alert.rule, alert.info.pid);
});

collector->start();
@endcode
*/
